**Part 4: CPU Architecture Optimization**

**Ideal CPU for Symbol-U**

Symbol-U benefits from **different** CPU characteristics than
transformers:

\# SYMBOL-U CPU REQUIREMENTS (Priority Order)

1\. LARGE L3 CACHE (critical)

\- Need: 256MB+ per socket

\- Why: Vritti lookup table, coupling matrices fit in cache

\- Impact: 10x faster than DRAM access

Example: AMD EPYC 9654 (384MB L3) vs Intel Xeon (105MB L3)

Symbol-U speedup: 2.5x on EPYC

2\. HIGH SINGLE-THREAD PERFORMANCE (critical)

\- Need: 4.5+ GHz boost, IPC \> 4.0

\- Why: Sequential operations (parsing, state machine)

\- Impact: 2x faster than low-freq server CPUs

Example: AMD Ryzen 9 7950X (5.7 GHz) vs Xeon (3.2 GHz)

Symbol-U speedup: 1.8x on Ryzen

3\. VECTOR INSTRUCTIONS (important)

\- Need: AVX-512 or AVX2 with good throughput

\- Why: Entropy computation, small matrix ops

\- Impact: 4x faster than scalar code

Example: Intel Xeon (AVX-512) vs ARM (NEON)

Symbol-U speedup: 3x on x86

4\. MANY CORES (moderate)

\- Need: 64-128 cores per socket

\- Why: Can parallelize across queries

\- Impact: Linear scaling up to core count

Example: Dual EPYC 9654 (192 cores) vs dual Xeon (64 cores)

Symbol-U throughput: 3x on EPYC

5\. MEMORY BANDWIDTH (less critical)

\- Need: 200+ GB/s per socket

\- Why: Most data fits in cache

\- Impact: Only matters for batch processing

